<!DOCTYPE html><html xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
<head>
  <title>VECDXF: VEC to DXF file conversion</title>
<meta content="text/html; charset=ISO-8859-1" http-equiv="Content-Type"/></head>

<body>
   <!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent al titol de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<h1><span id="wpstitol"/></h1>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent titol de la MSA editable de el WPS.-->
<!--Aquí inicia la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
<span id="wpsopcions"/>
<!--Aquí acaba la part corresponent a les opcions de de la MSA editable de el WPS.-->
  <p>ASCII polygons are converted to closed polylines; lines are converted to
  opened polylines; points can be converted to points or to texts. The maximum
  number of vertices in each line or polygon is 4.2 milion.<br/>
  The output DXF file contains a short header with its geographic
  boundaries.</p>

  <p>The program allows introducing terrain coordinates of the lower left
  corner to let DXF file to have map coordinates if it had not before, or to
  shift the whole drawing to a lower range of coordinates (for ex., some
  programs have problems while opening DXF files with UTM coordinates in
  m).<br/></p>

  <ul>
    <li style="list-style: none">Notes:</li>

    <li>Attributes become the names of the DXF layers.</li>

    <li>According to the DXF format, names of layers are transformed to
    capital letters and are truncated at 31 characters of length.</li>

    <li>Negative number attributes (for ex. holes) keep the sign in the
    name.</li>

    <li>Real attributes are only supported by option 3 of the program, because
    names of layers cannot contain decimal points.</li>

    <li>Range of numeric integer attributes allowed: -2147483648 to 2147483647
    (long).</li>
  </ul>
  <hr/>

  <exclusiva>
   <!-- Aquí inicia la part corresponent a la sintaxi de miramon. Aquesta part s'ha d'editar desde el document WPS (aplicacio.mps).-->
